[StringTable.1]
Reinforcements have arrived
[NewSubmission.Objectives]
The Germans have concentrated a large number of heavy tanks on your site. Your task is to repel all the attacks of the enemy's armored forces with the help of tank and artillery ambushes.
[NewSubmission.Description]
On December 26, 1944, the 2nd and 3rd Ukrainian Front completed the encirclement of the city of Budapest.
The German command began to prepare an operation to unblock the grouping of troops in Budapest. On January 2, the IV SS Panzer Corps, with the support of units of the 6th Army, launched an offensive in the defense zone of the 3rd Ukrainian Front. Fierce fighting ensued, and only by the beginning of February the German offensive was stopped.
On the morning of January 7, the Germans tried to make a breakthrough to Budapest through the positions of the 20th Guards Rifle Corps. For this purpose, two tank divisions, the 503 and 509 heavy tank battalions, the 2nd Hungarian Tank Division and separate tank battalions and assault gun brigades were concentrated.
Despite the good equipment of the 20th Guards Rifle Corps with artillery (including anti-tank), the Soviet command additionally transferred 2 cannon regiments and also put units of the 7th Mechanized Corps and the 1st Guards Mechanized Corps into battle.
The competent use of artillery and tanks by the defending Soviet troops made it possible to stop the German offensive by the end of the day.
[NewSubmission.Success]
[NewSubmission.Failed]
